WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.8 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Evaluation

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Evaluation asks whether your work achieves its outcomes and why: is it needed, and does it work?

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Evaluation asks deeper questions than monitoring: did the work achieve its outcomes, for whom, why, at what cost and with what unintended effects? For something new: is it needed, and does it work?

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Types for different purposes

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:37.130
Formative: Improves the work during delivery; it suits a pilot. For example: Mid-pilot chats with trainees to adjust shift times and training topics.

6
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:45.496
Process: Looks at how delivery works in practice. For example: Checking whether mentors follow the training plan and trainees keep attending.

7
00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:54.233
Summative: Judges results at the end of a period. For example: End-of-pilot review: did trainees finish, gain the certificate and find work?

8
00:00:54.233 --> 00:01:06.763
Impact: Estimates the difference made compared with what would otherwise have happened; usually comes later. For example: Years on, comparing trainees with similar young people who did not join.

9
00:01:07.163 --> 00:01:07.763
Why it matters

10
00:01:07.763 --> 00:01:13.437
1. It tells you whether to continue, change, scale up or stop.

11
00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:18.000
2. It finds unintended effects that monitoring can miss.

12
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.674
3. It gives funders and partners a credible story of your contribution.

13
00:01:25.074 --> 00:01:25.674
What it guides

14
00:01:25.674 --> 00:01:30.237
1. Your end-of-pilot review, run by you at first.

15
00:01:30.237 --> 00:01:35.170
2. Your bigger decisions: register, grow, change course or stop.

16
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:41.474
3. Your reports: findings, and how you responded to each one.

17
00:01:41.874 --> 00:01:42.474
What to avoid

18
00:01:42.474 --> 00:01:47.407
Covering all six criteria instead of your real questions.

19
00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:51.970
Promising rigorous impact evaluation you cannot yet afford.

20
00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:58.274
Finishing an evaluation with no plan to use its findings.

21
00:01:58.874 --> 00:02:00.674
You draft your evaluation plan for your pilot or first year.

22
00:02:00.674 --> 00:02:04.674
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:06.174 --> 00:02:09.274
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
